{"title":"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>With all angles measured in degrees, the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4e045d921715e2fe24a0647704f3bd4d19a51be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\prod_{k=1}^{45} \\csc^2(2k-1)^\\circ=m^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"178\" height=\"50\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are integers greater than 1. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/d/1adba016d140d37ff613ea8fdbb270450dbf7832.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\cos 1^\\circ + i \\sin 1^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"150\" height=\"14\" />. Then from the identity\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/9/9f9bac8ccb31b90efd23b31f531fc3d479844b63.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin 1 = \\frac{x - \\frac{1}{x}}{2i} = \\frac{x^2 - 1}{2 i x},\\]\" width=\"187\" height=\"40\" />\nwe deduce that (taking absolute values and noticing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/c/75c0d350ff15884b53791becb29db611a775b10d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x| = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />)\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd977b41090520cfe7f3703a585f036116db1872.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|2\\sin 1| = |x^2 - 1|.\\]\" width=\"141\" height=\"19\" />\nBut because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/1/9c1d35cfeba9718ae7f6c220e34b83c0dbd20669.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\csc$\" width=\"23\" height=\"8\" /> is the reciprocal of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb300dacfcde1b57ad070409262b1743e0cd966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" /> and because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/a/57a7dd14c0bb261b7b2f351a7125fe53793181f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin z = \\sin (180^\\circ - z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"160\" height=\"18\" />, if we let our product be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/1/641ac31f4882b96463aaf3c5df622e79b1654f33.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{M} = \\sin 1^\\circ \\sin 3^\\circ \\sin 5^\\circ \\dots \\sin 177^\\circ \\sin 179^\\circ\\]\" width=\"327\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/0/0f0c50deb3ec6dd601fd7d644416290c98fe749d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{1}{2^{90}} |x^2 - 1| |x^6 - 1| |x^{10} - 1| \\dots |x^{354} - 1| |x^{358} - 1|\\]\" width=\"400\" height=\"37\" />\nbecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb300dacfcde1b57ad070409262b1743e0cd966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" /> is positive in the first and second quadrants. Now, notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/7/627e1aedf429a8c113b7d0ed6446d413aed48d43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2, x^6, x^{10}, \\dots, x^{358}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" /> are the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9bf1a025bbc4637d569eec852eb8c1ef2e7c6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{90} + 1 = 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> Hence, we can write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/5/be5e526d64efd08d3053539529cafec4ff9d28ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(z - x^2)(z - x^6)\\dots (z - x^{358}) = z^{90} + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"312\" height=\"21\" />, and so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/1/8418b0ac667a85750f4bab65e2639648d7cc5c74.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{M} = \\dfrac{1}{2^{90}}|1 - x^2| |1 - x^6| \\dots |1 - x^{358}| = \\dfrac{1}{2^{90}} |1^{90} + 1| = \\dfrac{1}{2^{89}}.\\]\" width=\"462\" height=\"37\" />\nIt is easy to see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/9/6e98df5e08b9f07d57566f20d8ec9326559f3a32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M = 2^{89}$\" width=\"65\" height=\"15\" /> and that our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/e/aae06c6cc96bcbf5c4c2448dd21b96dd5a767360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 89 = \\boxed{091}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"114\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/9/c99d9afe8a3ed54dabb96c62aadf2a72a78b7a7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=\\sin1\\sin3\\sin5...\\sin89$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"205\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/1/2a126ddd6b2f9128981d4d1ebada9f7f8ed9520e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p=\\sqrt{\\sin1\\sin3\\sin5...\\sin177\\sin179}\\]\" width=\"286\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/effaa632edb0a78207b5cd85836dbb4d7b352176.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\sin1\\sin2\\sin3\\sin4...\\sin177\\sin178\\sin179}{\\sin2\\sin4\\sin6\\sin8...\\sin176\\sin178}}\\]\" width=\"369\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/a/06aa345e2e852655356e27b9bfe3ab24be1c61f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\sin1\\sin2\\sin3\\sin4...\\sin177\\sin178\\sin179}{(2\\sin1\\cos1)\\cdot(2\\sin2\\cos2)\\cdot(2\\sin3\\cos3)\\cdot....\\cdot(2\\sin89\\cos89)}}\\]\" width=\"532\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/0/000ae7ad249b7195b849703f5f46bd89f8f97e59.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2^{89}}\\frac{\\sin90\\sin91\\sin92\\sin93...\\sin177\\sin178\\sin179}{\\cos1\\cos2\\cos3\\cos4...\\cos89}}\\]\" width=\"432\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/e/b2e581d64a865a9c738e53c5a0932cb7d2e0f569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2^{89}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"64\" height=\"43\" /> because of the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/1/c61b318161aa513b5a2bfa73335e740db45b100f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(90+x)=\\cos(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/0/e109649eb2054c2d718dca51fc495ffffe914623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{p^2}=2^{89}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"66\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/3029cf102dbe49729574a92baa71868e36860409.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+89=\\boxed{091}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to Solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/d/16d78b66cd5fcbe8c350789c12cd41bc73244b02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{2\\theta}=2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta$\" width=\"153\" height=\"13\" /> and we find that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/8/358aff356066410bf9f69e48d3dbae6f138644fb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\sin(4)\\sin(8)\\sin(12)\\sin(16)\\cdots\\sin(84)\\sin(88)&amp;=(2\\sin(2)\\cos(2))(2\\sin(4)\\cos(4))(2\\sin(6)\\cos(6))(2\\sin(8)\\cos(8))\\cdots(2\\sin(42)\\cos(42))(2\\sin(44)\\cos(44))\\\\ &amp;=(2\\sin(2)\\sin(88))(2\\sin(4))\\sin(86))(2\\sin(6)\\sin(84))(2\\sin(8)\\sin(82))\\cdots(2\\sin(42)\\sin(48))(2\\sin(44)\\sin(46))\\\\ &amp;=2^{22}(\\sin(2)\\sin(88)\\sin(4)\\sin(86)\\sin(6)\\sin(84)\\sin(8)\\sin(82)\\cdots\\sin(42)\\sin(48)\\sin(44)\\sin(46))\\\\ &amp;=2^{22}(\\sin(2)\\sin(4)\\sin(6)\\sin(8)\\cdots\\sin(82)\\sin(84)\\sin(86)\\sin(88))\\end{align*}\" width=\"1200\" height=\"98\" />\nNow we can cancel the sines of the multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/5/675d147152b444555597d6b8319ae8a5d34fdf89.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1=2^{22}(\\sin(2)\\sin(6)\\sin(10)\\sin(14)\\cdots\\sin(82)\\sin(86))\\]\" width=\"416\" height=\"19\" />\nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/b/06b0c6062e11ecc01b80dd2e57f25365a9d6d049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(2)\\sin(6)\\sin(10)\\sin(14)\\cdots\\sin(82)\\sin(86)=2^{-22}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"405\" height=\"19\" /> and we can apply the double-angle formula again:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/0/a006661142727dcfefabc4bc73979404de97e5be.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}2^{-22}&amp;=(\\sin(2)\\sin(6)\\sin(10)\\sin(14)\\cdots\\sin(82)\\sin(86)\\\\ &amp;=(2\\sin(1)\\cos(1))(2\\sin(3)\\cos(3))(2\\sin(5)\\cos(5))(2\\sin(7)\\cos(7))\\cdots(2\\sin(41)\\cos(41))(2\\sin(43)\\cos(43))\\\\ &amp;=(2\\sin(1)\\sin(89))(2\\sin(3)\\sin(87))(2\\sin(5)\\sin(85))(2\\sin(7)\\sin(87))\\cdots(2\\sin(41)\\sin(49))(2\\sin(43)\\sin(47))\\\\ &amp;=2^{22}(\\sin(1)\\sin(89)\\sin(3)\\sin(87)\\sin(5)\\sin(85)\\sin(7)\\sin(83)\\cdots\\sin(41)\\sin(49)\\sin(43)\\sin(47))\\\\ &amp;=2^{22}(\\sin(1)\\sin(3)\\sin(5)\\sin(7)\\cdots\\sin(41)\\sin(43))(\\sin(47)\\sin(49)\\cdots\\sin(83)\\sin(85)\\sin(87)\\sin(89))\\end{align*}\" width=\"877\" height=\"125\" />\nOf course, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1beb8e5db30b286f39ec65bba7948c74eebace6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(45)=2^{-\\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"22\" /> is missing, so we multiply it to both sides:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea20eff96c6c859c0bb1977dcbf2909fc721c6e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{-22}\\sin(45)=2^{22}(\\sin(1)\\sin(3)\\sin(5)\\sin(7)\\cdots\\sin(41)\\sin(43))(\\sin(45))(\\sin(47)\\sin(49)\\cdots\\sin(83)\\sin(85)\\sin(87)\\sin(89))\\]\" width=\"931\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/1/ed1cb506c4db8b8c769de081cba17d76eec94689.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(2^{-22}\\right)\\left(2^{-\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)=2^{22}(\\sin(1)\\sin(3)\\sin(5)\\sin(7)\\cdots\\sin(83)\\sin(85)\\sin(87)\\sin(89))\\]\" width=\"607\" height=\"32\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/5/7552afac43b9e498ea75fd27900a3c7f34cfcf0f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{-\\frac{45}{2}}=2^{22}(\\sin(1)\\sin(3)\\sin(5)\\sin(7)\\cdots\\sin(83)\\sin(85)\\sin(87)\\sin(89))\\]\" width=\"541\" height=\"22\" />\nNow isolate the product of the sines:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195034d13a50fbfbb934b3a6ffd72fa057f2c714.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(1)\\sin(3)\\sin(5)\\sin(7)\\cdots\\sin(83)\\sin(85)\\sin(87)\\sin(89)=2^{-\\frac{89}{2}}\\]\" width=\"503\" height=\"22\" />\nAnd the product of the squares of the cosecants as asked for by the problem is the square of the inverse of this number:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/710932d64f6a9dd85c4fb20b6c47dc22d75e92d6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\csc^2(1)\\csc^2(3)\\csc^2(5)\\csc^2(7)\\cdots\\csc^2(83)\\csc^2(85)\\csc^2(87)\\csc^2(89)=\\left(\\frac{1}{2^{-\\frac{89}{2}}}\\right)^2=\\left(2^{\\frac{89}{2}}\\right)^2=2^{89}\\]\" width=\"734\" height=\"46\" />\nThe answer is therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/8/258f52b67c1f60aec3b5b87d0962ea30c2b217c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n=(2)+(89)=\\boxed{091}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"214\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee850685f9beb544834fb2be48f7cdfba4394f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=\\prod_{k=1}^{45} \\csc^2(2k-1)^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"163\" height=\"50\" />.\n</p><p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33cb7d15dd7ba3ea999b8fbce08620ca5cf6e27e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{p}}=\\prod_{k=1}^{45} \\sin(2k-1)^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"175\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/a/13a32c653b2cceb70bd04aeaa28e31cec757b1fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\theta=\\cos(90^{\\circ}-\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"18\" />, we can multiply both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/7/cc7c4b51e06b26289d792878cbf9efac28aac903.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/5/d65ad0b6aea923547e2e04fd973bd3268713fe7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2p}}=\\prod_{k=1}^{23} \\sin(2k-1)^\\circ\\cos(2k-1)^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"283\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p>Using the double-angle identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/1/f01adb31b1a34033ea77e80e94f8032dee63705f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin2\\theta=2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta$\" width=\"153\" height=\"13\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5af7fdbc0534340701f8d4459746a7f58243c139.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2p}}=\\frac{1}{2^{23}}\\prod_{k=1}^{23} \\sin(4k-2)^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"214\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p>Note that the right-hand side is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/c/50c9cf03f799c2239cff0f0660a9c8e797e374b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2^{23}}\\prod_{k=1}^{45} \\sin(2k)^\\circ\\div \\prod_{k=1}^{22} \\sin(4k)^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"231\" height=\"50\" />, which is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae72e4d6cb66fd4afae164835880f2d21ca11e4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2^{23}}\\prod_{k=1}^{45} \\sin(2k)^\\circ\\div \\prod_{k=1}^{22} 2\\sin(2k)^\\circ\\cos(2k)^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"315\" height=\"56\" />, again, from using our double-angle identity.\n</p><p>Putting this back into our equation and simplifying gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/4/2e4092455317b9babe8a08a099afc9afc7d65cf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2p}}=\\frac{1}{2^{45}}\\prod_{k=23}^{45} \\sin(2k)^\\circ\\div \\prod_{k=1}^{22} \\cos(2k)^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"304\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p>Using the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/a/13a32c653b2cceb70bd04aeaa28e31cec757b1fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\theta=\\cos(90^{\\circ}-\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"18\" /> again, our equation simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/0/c402296137874edd573e4f8947340ebd621557a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2p}}=\\frac{\\sin90^\\circ}{2^{45}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"117\" height=\"53\" />, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/c/3ccaada55abc58c5a0f70df67af7b715d4c0e4a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin90^\\circ=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/6/be65820da355671fc4a66b4f5eb675bb415c743b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2p = 2^{90}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />, which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cd0f27474cb0c9c829c153671469c35bc811769.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=2^{89}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/9/e799c5fa26da35117407dd70b76479e47a7a0d37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n=2+89=\\boxed{091}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"186\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Once we have the tools of complex polynomials there is no need to use the tactical tricks. Everything is so basic (I think).\n</p><p>Recall that the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/e/8debda55cb36e43070d67f9efd56e1f7084cc0ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/c/48cacf4dbd3b8d5fde459357c4f94a855fc78820.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{\\frac{(2k-1)\\pi i}{n}}, k=1,2,...,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"171\" height=\"24\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/d/65d2fe4109567c71f6327e6f10b78b79d5a0ca2e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^n + 1 = \\prod_{k=1}^{n}(x-e^{\\frac{(2k-1)\\pi i}{n}})\\]\" width=\"204\" height=\"48\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, and take absolute value of both sides,  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4373a48f44f9e8b95e397e2003b64464247ed5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 = \\prod_{k=1}^{n}|1-e^{\\frac{(2k-1)\\pi i}{n}}|= 2^n\\prod_{k=1}^{n}|\\sin\\frac{(2k-1)\\pi}{2n}|\\]\" width=\"350\" height=\"48\" />\nor, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/2/40261dc747a132117a4c313f61f7f95bc6e8c112.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\prod_{k=1}^{n}|\\sin\\frac{(2k-1)\\pi}{2n}| = 2^{-(n-1)}\\]\" width=\"222\" height=\"48\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be even, then,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/b/03b96124a4191e3fd4dc1d73deeb3d149520d06e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin\\frac{(2k-1)\\pi}{2n} = \\sin\\left(\\pi - \\frac{(2k-1)\\pi}{2n}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\frac{(2(n-k+1)-1)\\pi}{2n}\\right)\\]\" width=\"523\" height=\"43\" />\nso,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/b/65bbaeb84064c3ed19d30c17caab473da8bd2e1e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\prod_{k=1}^{n}\\left|\\sin\\frac{(2k-1)\\pi}{n}\\right| = \\prod_{k=1}^{\\frac{n}{2}}\\sin^2\\frac{(2k-1)\\pi}{2n}\\]\" width=\"305\" height=\"53\" />\nSet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16e09f4325b765617c0f76004b9cd4c185f049a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=90$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> and we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/9/979f740e401c5741b6f506eb612e77bb7c505d58.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\prod_{k=1}^{45}\\sin^2\\frac{(2k-1)\\pi}{180} = 2^{-89}\\]\" width=\"195\" height=\"50\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/5/1e55433be8f84f2b2b29b9b95a317bbc912f383e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\prod_{k=1}^{45}\\csc^2\\frac{(2k-1)\\pi}{180} = 2^{89}\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"50\" />\n-Mathdummy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Recall that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/c/87c3ad30490063476be9db2f9be9044b6f4d5f04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\alpha\\cdot \\sin(60^{\\circ}-\\alpha)\\cdot \\sin(60^{\\circ}+\\alpha)=\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\sin3\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"354\" height=\"38\" />\nSince it is in csc, we can write in sin and then take reciprocal.\nWe can group them by threes, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d12240e5e6879a1c2826daed35ab2d6468e439e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=(\\sin1^{\\circ}\\cdot \\sin59^{\\circ}\\cdot \\sin61^{\\circ})\\cdots(\\sin29^{\\circ}\\cdot \\sin31^{\\circ}\\cdot \\sin89^{\\circ})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"446\" height=\"20\" />. Thus\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/3/433fccc092c4168b030a5d21d32e3b78b76d3ac6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} P &amp;=\\frac{1}{4^{15}}\\cdot \\sin3^{\\circ}\\cdot \\sin9^{\\circ}\\cdots\\sin87^{\\circ}\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{1}{4^{20}}\\cdot \\sin9^{\\circ}\\cdot \\sin27^{\\circ}\\cdot \\sin45^{\\circ}\\cdot \\sin63^{\\circ}\\cdot \\sin81^{\\circ}\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{1}{4^{20}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\sin9^{\\circ}\\cdot \\cos9^{\\circ}\\cdot \\sin27^{\\circ}\\cdot \\cos27^{\\circ}\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{1}{4^{21}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\sin18^{\\circ}\\cdot \\cos36^{\\circ}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2^{45}} \\end{align*}\" width=\"375\" height=\"176\" />\nSo we take reciprocal, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/5411f7d2fa505893859755ad0c7485ee34a0a54b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 1P=2^{\\frac{89}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"38\" />, the desired answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bff7bee7b107d4263e6779a324b92b0055684be2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{P^2}=2^{89}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"75\" height=\"38\" /> leads to answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accb5449e284cb0b95b5ec7be33860ba136c18de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{091}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~bluesoul\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/d/a2dbe40c8052f19dfff393a1f320b58aa04c6911.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\prod_{k=1}^{45} \\csc^2(2k-1)^\\circ = \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sin1^\\circ \\cdot \\sin3^\\circ \\cdots \\sin89^\\circ}\\right)^2.\\]\" width=\"374\" height=\"51\" />\n</p><p>Multiplying by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/b/19b6adee952c7d0e987b02df716b814055472228.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sin2^\\circ \\cdot \\sin4^\\circ \\cdots \\sin88^\\circ}{\\sin2^\\circ \\cdot \\sin4^\\circ \\cdots \\sin88^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"182\" height=\"39\" /> gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6871bc9a7bfc208a755df09a500e001423cc51f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{\\sin2^\\circ \\cdot \\sin4^\\circ \\cdots \\sin88^\\circ}{\\sin1^\\circ \\sin2^\\circ \\cdot \\sin3^\\circ \\cdots \\sin88^\\circ \\cdot \\sin89^\\circ}\\right)^2\\]\" width=\"318\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/d/f9d2370e973a132988647941d748840c85e13cb9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\left(\\frac{\\sin2^\\circ \\cdot \\sin4^\\circ \\cdots \\sin88^\\circ}{\\sin1^\\circ \\sin2^\\circ \\cdot \\sin3^\\circ \\cdots \\sin 45^\\circ \\cdot \\cos 44^\\circ \\cdot \\cos 43^\\circ \\cdots \\cos1^\\circ}\\right)^2.\\]\" width=\"487\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>Using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/689411ffbc559bfbabd1d59ba697522b2b0dca7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\alpha \\cos\\alpha = \\frac{1}{2}\\sin{2\\alpha}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"167\" height=\"38\" /> gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/b/f2b53b286c91f7acc1a2c85066423059919bfc1f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{\\sin2^\\circ \\cdot \\sin4^\\circ \\cdots \\sin88^\\circ}{\\frac{1}{2} \\sin2^\\circ \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\sin4^\\circ \\cdots \\frac{1}{2} \\sin88^\\circ \\cdot \\sin45^\\circ}\\right) ^2\\]\" width=\"313\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb0193505f2ab32d58acbc993d533f6a97af03ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\left(\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{2})^{44} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}}\\right)^2\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/3/c8373816f2b905a6a4426f2d762c0c5615441d44.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 2^{89}.\\]\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/5/2c5003e74dc1dc1a59a32f65438e02e6edef1abb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+89 = \\boxed{091}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"119\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8\">Solution 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/d/5bd8c114a2fb4f12a55c42c23d0f423cd36edae2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\prod_{k=1}^{45} \\csc^2(2k-1) = \\prod_{k=45}^{1} \\sec^2(2k-1) = \\prod_{k=1}^{45} \\sec^2(2k-1) =  \\prod_{k=1}^{45} (1+\\tan^2(2k-1))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"617\" height=\"56\" /> \nHowever, note that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> numbers in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/524ada669a2eb77641874d25196d9a35d1594774.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\tan^2(2k-1)} = \\tan(2k-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"233\" height=\"35\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/a/5da037fff59974862964c5e6e92e7f4be8b83126.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le{k}\\le{45}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" /> are precisely the roots of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88c01bb54e8e2567b4ab420168ec1534d6ffabf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\tan{(\\tan^{-1}{90x}})} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"158\" height=\"43\" />. Thus, it suffices to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/a/0eadb50cf56185ae8434a937d4008d6fc80f1be2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|P(-1)|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the polynomial formed by the denominator of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36fd0daa5f195c39767b4bedc34ec0c16c2a596b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{(\\tan^{-1}{90\\sqrt{x}})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"22\" />. This is true because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/5/bf5d0ac6f00cfdf1c8c34ebdcaead95fe0525487.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\prod_{k=1}^{45} (x-\\tan^2(2k-1)) = \\prod_{k=1}^{45} -(-x+\\tan^2(2k-1))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"396\" height=\"56\" /> gives us the factored root form of the equation where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is undefined, which corresponds to the equation where the denominator equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>It remains to find the denominator of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />; fortunately, we may use tangent angle multiplication rules. Specifically, the denominator of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/3/ff35ce4b9b380eb758a35cd021c28101f442a01d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{n=0} ^{45} (-1)^n\\binom{90}{2n}\\sqrt{x}^{2n} = \\sum_{n=0} ^{45} (-1)^n\\binom{90}{2n}x^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"327\" height=\"55\" />. Evaluating at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/4/8d4c38a419ae56f13a202216dd45a1978bc91a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />, we may obtain the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/f/bcf952cc32635b83f0117aa83b66e9f7231d2657.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{n=0} ^{45} (-1)^n\\binom{90}{2n}(-1)^{n} = \\sum_{n=0} ^{45} \\binom{90}{2n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"270\" height=\"55\" />. \n</p><p>From here, there are two ways to finish; the first is to recognize the well known sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/b/7cb3e3fd1a2cb2f7c5ceb70a57f7f1cb409b001c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{n=0} ^{k} \\binom{2k}{2n} = 2^(2k-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"176\" height=\"56\" />, from which we may plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/8/ae872ae69c28e0be6a562aa2fa3f02ef93f67bc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" /> to see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601d1911eef7d56783305f8dc7717762c8c61b65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|P(-1)| = 2^(45*2-1) = 2^{89}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"233\" height=\"23\" /> to obtain the answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/3029cf102dbe49729574a92baa71868e36860409.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+89=\\boxed{091}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />. Otherwise, you may split the previous sum; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/2/0d2e596f81c56ebe22fc2834d912cc1369882014.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{n=0} ^{45} \\binom{90}{2n} = \\sum_{n=0} ^{45} \\binom{89}{2n-1} + \\binom{89}{2n} = \\sum_{n=0} ^{89} \\binom{89}{n} = 2^{89}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"428\" height=\"55\" />, which also gives the correct answer. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_9\">Solution 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We begin by computing\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/8/a4845c1bcbddaa9e1d4e2bc284ac73edb185b8e6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\prod_{k=1}^{90}\\sin{k^{\\circ}}\\right)^2=\\prod_{k=1}^{179}\\sin{k^{\\circ}}\\]\" width=\"194\" height=\"57\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/7/e1799e372708bdf24115e4d32610344555d849be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{1}=e^{i1^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"21\" />. Using the Euler's Formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/0/4f08dab7ede7e4ec9886e89c74186caa1b2cccab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\theta}=\\frac{e^{i\\theta}-e^{-i\\theta}}{2i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"138\" height=\"41\" />, it follows that\n\\begin{align*}\n\\prod_{k=1}^{179}\\sin{k^{\\circ}}&amp;=\\frac{(z_{1}-\\frac{1}{z_{1}})(z_{1}^{2}-\\frac{1}{z_{1}^{2}})\\ldots (z_{1}^{179}-\\frac{1}{z_{1}^{179}})}{-2^{179}i}\\\\\n&amp;=\\frac{(1-z_{1}^{2})(1-z_{1}^{4})\\ldots (1-z_{1}^{358})}{-(-1)^{179}\\cdot z_{1}^{90\\cdot 179}2^{179}i}\\\\\n&amp;=\\frac{(1-z_{1}^{2})(1-z_{1}^{4})\\ldots (1-z_{1}^{358})}{2^{179}}\n\\end{align*}\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/d/46d8af88876d94e389e51ddf776f06d6294b792f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=\\frac{x^{180}-1}{x-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"128\" height=\"42\" />. Factoring by the Fundamental Theorem of Algebra and roots of unity, we find\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/3/a03dfc6b0c1872cde43927c970d6f88f4a3e9c24.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x)=(x-z_{1}^{2})(x-z_{1}^{4})\\ldots (x-z_{1}^{358})=1+x+x^2+\\ldots +x^{179}\\]\" width=\"491\" height=\"20\" />\nThus,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/1/961ba2300c44b28ef5e74e5196dacfc600912333.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\prod_{k=1}^{179}\\sin{k^{\\circ}}=\\frac{f(1)}{2^{179}}=\\frac{180}{2^{179}}\\]\" width=\"188\" height=\"51\" />\nWe proceed by computing\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/c/f5c78f59c8b6d1dc7a937dd0e6c0c484976084b0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\prod_{k=1}^{45}\\sin{2k^{\\circ}}\\right)^{2}=\\prod_{k=1}^{89}\\sin{2k^{\\circ}}\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"57\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601be566c80af7c831913c65be4a6d85191b485d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{2}=e^{i2^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"21\" />. We have\n\\begin{align*}\n\\prod_{k=1}^{89}\\sin{2k^{\\circ}}&amp;=\\frac{(z_{2}-\\frac{1}{z_{2}})(z_{2}^{2}-\\frac{1}{z_{2}^{2}})\\ldots (z_{1}^{89}-\\frac{1}{z_{1}^{89}})}{2^{89}i}\\\\\n&amp;=\\frac{(1-z_{1}^{2})(1-z_{1}^{4})\\ldots (1-z_{1}^{178})}{(-1)^{89}\\cdot z_{1}^{45\\cdot 89}2^{89}i}\\\\\n&amp;=\\frac{(1-z_{1}^{2})(1-z_{1}^{4})\\ldots (1-z_{1}^{178})}{2^{89}}\n\\end{align*}\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/c/eccd90ef048babe1c5c234d5a5e2eb645221abbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)=\\frac{x^{90}-1}{x-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"120\" height=\"42\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/d/1edef9ee973ef2a1543395993f64213e1193502c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g(x)=(x-z_{2}^{2})(x-z_{2}^{4})\\ldots (x-z_{2}^{178})=1+x+x^2+\\ldots +x^{89}\\]\" width=\"483\" height=\"20\" />\nHence,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b45cc3f9427d6d49b66aafd2272df640cd79cd8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\prod_{k=1}^{89}\\sin{2k^{\\circ}}=\\frac{g(1)}{2^{89}}=\\frac{90}{2^{89}}\\]\" width=\"189\" height=\"51\" />\nTherefore, the desired product evaluates to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02e2b86756839b34df3ffbbacfd7e8f0f5e9829a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\prod_{k=1}^{45} \\csc^2(2k-1)^\\circ=\\frac{\\left(\\prod_{k=1}^{45}\\sin{2k^{\\circ}}\\right)^{2}}{\\left(\\prod_{k=1}^{90}\\sin{k^{\\circ}}\\right)^2}=\\frac{90}{2^{89}}\\cdot \\frac{2^{179}}{180}=2^{89}\\]\" width=\"427\" height=\"76\" />\nThe requested sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/3029cf102dbe49729574a92baa71868e36860409.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+89=\\boxed{091}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~Pieandpi31415926535897932\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I\" title=\"2015 AIME I\">2015 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2015\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016235938\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.067 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.134 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 709/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1790/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 112/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 27457/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.220      1 -total\n 59.68%    8.486      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.74%    5.509      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14104:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016235938 and revision id 287911. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}